# Copy this file to backend/.env and fill in your own values.
# backend/.env is gitignored — never commit real credentials.

# --- Supabase Postgres ---------------------------------------------------
# In the Supabase dashboard: Connect (top bar) -> Connection string.
#
# Pick "Session pooler". On the free tier the Direct connection is IPv6-only
# (IPv4 is a paid add-on), so on a typical home or campus network it fails with
# "could not translate host name" or "Network is unreachable". The session
# pooler is IPv4 on every tier and is meant for long-lived servers like this one.
#
# Do NOT use the Transaction pooler (port 6543) here — it is for serverless,
# and it does not support prepared statements.
#
# Shape (note the dot in the username, and port 5432):
#   postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
#
# If your password contains @ : / ? # or %, percent-encode it, otherwise the
# URL parses wrongly (e.g. @ becomes %40).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.your-project-ref:your-password@aws-0-your-region.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"

# --- Official X API (optional) -------------------------------------------
# Only needed for x_api_search.py, which pulls recent vaccine posts through the
# official API. The rest of the app (x_post_fetcher.py) needs no credentials.
#
# From developer.x.com: create a project + app, then copy its Bearer Token.
#
# NOTE: the X API is pay-per-usage with no free tier — roughly $0.005 per post
# returned. x_api_search.py ranks a pool of posts locally because the API cannot
# sort by view count, so a 100-post pool costs about $0.50 per run.
X_BEARER_TOKEN=""

# --- Apify (optional) ----------------------------------------------------
# Only needed for backend/main_api/apify/, the fallback collector. It runs the
# apidojo/tweet-scraper Actor instead of the official X API.
#
# Why a fallback exists: the official full-archive endpoint (x_historical_search)
# needs a Self-serve or Enterprise entitlement the default pay-per-use plan does
# not include, so it answers 403. Apify needs no such upgrade.
#
# Token: https://console.apify.com/settings/integrations
#
# NOTE: Apify bills about $0.40 per 1,000 tweets - roughly a twelfth of the
# official API's $5.00 per 1,000. The free tier allows 5 runs a month capped at
# 10 items each, which is enough to smoke-test but not to collect with.
APIFY_TOKEN=""
